      "problem": "Express $P(x)⇔Q(x)$ as a sentence given the following notations:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is positive.\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x>0.$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's recall the following grammatical constructions for the biconditional $P⇔Q:$\n\n- $P$ if and only if $Q$\n\n- $P$ iff $Q$\n\n- $P$ is necessary and sufficient for $Q$\n\n- $P$ is equivalent to $Q$\n\n- If $P$ then $Q,$ and conversely\n\nTherefore, among the given options, the grammatical construction of $P(x)⇔Q(x)$ is the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x$ is positive **is equivalent to** $x>0.$",
